  "result": "This confirms it: `webhook-delivery-job.ts` is self-contained — it defines `MAX_ATTEMPTS` and `backoffMs` locally and doesn't import from `queue.ts` or `constants.ts`, so this is the actual file governing retry count and wait growth for messages queued to a customer's receiving server.\n\nTaskflow's webhook delivery retries — the scenario of a customer's receiving server being down and Taskflow retrying queued messages with growing waits before giving up on the oldest ones — is governed entirely by `src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts`. It defines `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 6` (the retry ceiling, checked at line 49 to mark a delivery permanently failed) and the exponential `backoffMs()` function (lines 89–93), which doubles the wait each attempt (1s, 2s, 4s, …) capped at 5 minutes. Note `src/config/constants.ts` has an unused `WEBHOOK_MAX_ATTEMPTS = 5` constant that this job doesn't actually reference, and `src/server/jobs/queue.ts` has its own separate generic retry/backoff (5 attempts, 1-minute cap) for other job kinds — neither of those governs webhook delivery specifically.\n\nANSWER: src/server/jobs/webhook-delivery-job.ts",
